{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Amend the law to allow for tenants to leave with less than 2 months\u2019 notice",
        "additional_details": "These changes would require written clarity on surrender, returned keys and remaining rent, and prohibit overlapping rent charges after a replacement tenancy begins. We believe tenants should not have to choose between unsafe housing and paying rent on two homes. \r\n\r\nFamilies with children can face particular hardship. We want a clear early exit right, defined evidence requirements and a rapid independent process for disputes. A standard written surrender procedure should\r\nconfirm the tenancy end date and any remaining rent liability when keys are returned. Deposit deductions should require clear reasons and evidence.\r\n",
        "background": "Amend the two-month notice rule under the Renters\u2019 Rights Act 2025 to allow tenants to leave with less than two months\u2019 notice where serious housing hazards or material misrepresentation are established.",
